      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Preventing surface dulling is definitely achievable, though it requires a proactive approach, not just a passive one. For the polished concrete, the key is a high-quality, durable sealer—not just a basic wax, but a penetrating epoxy or urethane sealer that locks the surface down. With natural stone, you need a professional, high-solids impregnating sealer applied correctly to repel etching from acidic spills and minimize the ingress of abrasive grit. These protective layers act as a barrier, significantly slowing down the visual degradation caused by daily foot traffic.",
